Print the line that turns on Tab completion for tasqx.

It writes one line to stdout, so `tasqx completions bash >> ~/.bashrc` works.

Usage: tasqx completions [OPTIONS] [SHELL]

Arguments:
  [SHELL]
          Which shell (bash, elvish, fish, powershell, zsh). Detected from $SHELL when omitted; on Windows nothing sets $SHELL, so name it

Options:
      --json
          Print the raw JSON API result instead of the human table

      --theme <THEME>
          Theme name (built-in nord|gruvbox|dracula|solarized|mono, or a user file). Overrides $TASQX_THEME and the config file (DESIGN.md §8)

      --socket <SOCKET>
          Local socket / named-pipe address of a tasqx daemon. Overrides $TASQX_SOCK. When a daemon is reachable, one-shot commands route through it (single writer); otherwise they run in-process. A set $TASQX_DB naming a different store than that daemon's is refused. Also selects the address for `daemon` and `watch`

      --no-daemon
          Never route through a daemon; always run one-shot in-process (the pre-daemon behaviour). Escape hatch for scripts

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

EXAMPLES
  tasqx completions bash
  tasqx completions bash >> ~/.bashrc    # the printed line is one line for exactly this

NOTE  tasqx never edits a startup file: add the printed line yourself. `tasqx manual completion` names the file for each shell.

See also: manual · docs        Full manual: tasqx manual
